      "text": "The ego depletion hypothesis holds that acts of self-control draw on a limited resource that is diminished by prior exertion.",
      "factual": true,
      "stance": "asserted"
    },
    {
      "id": "a1",
      "pos": 2,
      "text": "Baumeister, Bratslavsky, Muraven, and Tice published the original ego depletion experiments in 1998.",
      "factual": true,
      "stance": "asserted"
    },
    {
      "id": "a2",
      "pos": 3,
      "text": "Hagger and colleagues published a Registered Replication Report on ego depletion in 2016.",
      "factual": true,
      "stance": "asserted"
    },
    {
      "id": "a3",
      "pos": 4,
      "text": "The 2016 Registered Replication Report comprised 23 separate laboratories.",
      "factual": true,
      "stance": "asserted"
    },
    {
      "id": "a4",
      "pos": 5,
      "text": "The 2016 Registered Replication Report was published in Nature Human Behaviour.",
      "factual": false,
      "stance": "asserted"
    },
